+//! The iteration helpers and memoisation added by phase-098.
+//!
+//! Redblue lists are values, so every helper here answers a new list rather
+//! than an iterator. The tests pin the three shapes the phase requires —
+//! empty, one element and many — and run each helper on both engines, because
+//! the tree-walker is the reference and the bytecode VM has to agree with it.
+//!
+//! `lru_cache` is pinned by counting calls, not only by comparing results: a
+//! cache that never hits returns the same answers as one that works, and only
+//! the call count tells the two apart. The eviction test asserts the count
+//! rises again after the capacity is passed, which is what distinguishes a
+//! bound from an unbounded memo.
+
